{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:Install\\-TransportAgent)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Tobias Michalski (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the Installation of a Exchange Transport Agent (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_msexchange_transport_agent.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: MSExchange Transport Agent Installation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1505.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1 and $selection_commandline_all2 and $selection_commandline_all3)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\reg\\.exe$)'", "$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:query)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\\\software\\\\)'", "$selection_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/v)'", "$selection_commandline_all3: CommandLine ~= '(?i:svcversion)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nikita Nazarov, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may attempt to enumerate software for a variety of reasons, such as figuring out what security measures are present or if the compromised system has a version of software that is vulnerable. (source: proc_creation_win_reg_software_discovery.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Detected Windows Software Discovery", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1518"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_pipename)", "Matches": ["$selection_pipename: PipeName ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\imposecost)|(?i:\\\\imposingcost))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects creation of default named pipes used by the Koh tool (source: pipe_created_hktl_koh_default_pipe.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 9, "EventIDs": [17, 18], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: HackTool - Koh Default Named Pipe", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1528", "T1134.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\shutdown\\.exe$)'", "$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:/r\\ )|(?i:/s\\ ))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Use of the commandline to shutdown or reboot windows (source: proc_creation_win_shutdown_execution.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Execution of Shutdown", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1529"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\wpbbin\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects creation of a file named \"wpbbin\" in the \"%systemroot%\\system32\\\" directory. Which could be indicative of UEFI based persistence method (source: file_event_win_wpbbin_persistence.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: UEFI Persistence Via Wpbbin - FileCreation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1542.001"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_imageloaded) or ($selection_2_hashes))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?i:\\\\kprocesshacker\\.sys$)'", "$selection_2_hashes: Hashes ~= '(?:(?i:IMPHASH=821D74031D3F625BCBD0DF08B70F1E77)|(?i:IMPHASH=F86759BB4DE4320918615DC06E998A39)|(?i:IMPHASH=0A64EEB85419257D0CE32BD5D55C3A18)|(?i:IMPHASH=6E7B34DFC017700B1517B230DF6FF0D0))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects driver load of the Process Hacker tool (source: driver_load_win_pua_process_hacker.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [6], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PUA - Process Hacker Driver Load", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1543"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_imageloaded)", "Matches": ["$selection_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?i:\\\\Temp\\\\)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects a driver load from a temporary directory (source: driver_load_win_susp_temp_use.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [6], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Driver Load From A Temporary Directory", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1543.003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Software\\\\Classes\\\\Folder\\\\shell\\\\open\\\\command\\\\DelegateExecute)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Omkar Gudhate", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects changes to 'HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\Folder\\shell\\open\\command\\DelegateExecute' (source: registry_set_comhijack_sdclt.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: COM Hijack via Sdclt", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546", "T1548"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject) and ! ($filter_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Control\\ Panel\\\\Desktop\\\\SCRNSAVE\\.EXE$)'", "$filter_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\rundll32\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\explorer\\.exe$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Bartlomiej Czyz @bczyz1, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects value modification of registry key containing path to binary used as screensaver. (source: registry_event_modify_screensaver_binary_path.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Path To Screensaver Binary Modified", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_imageloaded)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\wbem\\\\WmiPrvSE\\.exe$)'", "$selection_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?i:\\\\wbemcons\\.dll$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Thomas Patzke", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects WMI command line event consumers (source: image_load_wmi_persistence_commandline_event_consumer.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [7], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: WMI Persistence - Command Line Event Consumer", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1 and $selection_commandline_all2)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:copy\\ )'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/y\\ )'", "$selection_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:C:\\\\windows\\\\system32\\\\cmd\\.exe\\ C:\\\\windows\\\\system32\\\\sethc\\.exe)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Sreeman", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "By replacing the sticky keys executable with the local admins CMD executable, an attacker is able to access a privileged windows console session without authenticating to the system.\nWhen the sticky keys are \"activated\" the privilleged shell is launched.\n (source: proc_creation_win_cmd_sticky_keys_r", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 9, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Persistence Via Sticky Key Backdoor", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.008"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_targetobject) or ($selection_2_newname))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:^HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\Session\\ Manager\\\\AppCertDlls$)'", "$selection_2_newname: NewName ~= '(?i:^HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\Session\\ Manager\\\\AppCertDlls$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Ilyas Ochkov, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Dynamic-link libraries (DLLs) that are specified in the AppCertDLLs value in the Registry key can be abused to obtain persistence and privilege escalation\nby causing a malicious DLL to be loaded and run in the context of separate processes on the computer.\n (source: registry_event_new_dll_added_to_a", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: New DLL Added to AppCertDlls Registry Key", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.009"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_targetobject) or ($selection_2_newname)) and ! ($filter_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_1_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Windows\\\\AppInit_Dlls$)|(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Wow6432Node\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Windows\\\\AppInit_Dlls$))'", "$selection_2_newname: NewName ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Windows\\\\AppInit_Dlls$)|(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Wow6432Node\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Windows\\\\AppInit_Dlls$))'", "$filter_details: Details ~= '(?i:^\\(Empty\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Ilyas Ochkov, oscd.community, Tim Shelton", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "DLLs that are specified in the AppInit_DLLs value in the Registry key HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Windows are loaded by user32.dll into every process that loads user32.dll (source: registry_event_new_dll_added_to_appinit_dlls_registry_key.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: New DLL Added to AppInit_DLLs Registry Key", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.010"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_targetobject_2)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\AppCompatFlags\\\\Custom\\\\)'", "$selection_targetobject_2: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\csrss\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\dllhost\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\explorer\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\RuntimeBroker\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\services\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\sihost\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\svchost\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\taskhostw\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\winlogon\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\WmiPrvSe\\.exe$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects installation of new shim databases that try to patch sections of known processes for potential process injection or persistence. (source: registry_set_persistence_shim_database_susp_application.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Shim Database Patching Activity", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.011"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_targetobject_2 and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\App\\ Paths)'", "$selection_targetobject_2: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\(Default\\)$)|(?i:Path$))'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Users\\\\Public)|(?i:\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Windows\\\\Temp\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Desktop\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Downloads\\\\)|(?i:%temp%)|(?i:%tmp%)|(?i:iex)|(?i:Invoke\\-)|(?i:rundll32)|(?i:regsvr32)|(?i:mshta)|(?i:cscript)|(?i:wscript)|(?i:\\.bat)|(?i:\\.hta)|(?i:\\.dll)|(?i:\\.ps1))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects changes to the \"Default\" property for keys located in the \\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths\\ registry. Which might be used as a method of persistence\nThe entries found under App Paths are used primarily for the following purposes.\nFirst, to map an application's executable ", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Persistence Via App Paths Default Property", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.012"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\.PowerShell_profile\\.ps1$)|(?i:\\\\PowerShell\\\\profile\\.ps1$)|(?i:\\\\Program\\ Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\-preview\\\\profile\\.ps1$)|(?i:\\\\Program\\ Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\profile\\.ps1$)|(?i:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1\\.0\\\\profile\\.ps1$)|(?i:\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\profile\\.ps1$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "HieuTT35, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the creation or modification of a powershell profile which could indicate suspicious activity as the profile can be used as a mean of persistence (source: file_event_win_susp_powershell_profile.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PowerShell Profile Modification", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.013"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:InprocServer32\\\\\\(Default\\)$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\system32\\\\scrobj\\.dll$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detect use of scrobj.dll as this DLL looks for the ScriptletURL key to get the location of the script to execute (source: registry_set_persistence_scrobj_dll.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Persistence Via Scrobj.dll COM Hijacking", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.015"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename_all0 and $selection_targetfilename_all1 and $selection_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename_all0: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\Start\\ Menu\\\\Programs\\\\Startup)'", "$selection_targetfilename_all1: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\.lnk\\.\\{0AFACED1\\-E828\\-11D1\\-9187\\-B532F1E9575D\\})'", "$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\explorer\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Greg (rule)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects a phishing attack which expands a ZIP file containing a malicious shortcut.\nIf the victim expands the ZIP file via the explorer process, then the explorer process expands the malicious ZIP file and drops a malicious shortcut redirected to a backdoor into the Startup folder.\nAdditionally, the", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential RipZip Attack on Startup Folder", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\msdt\\.exe$)'", "$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Desktop\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Start\\ Menu\\\\Programs\\\\Startup\\\\)|(?i:C:\\\\PerfLogs\\\\)|(?i:C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\)|(?i:C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Vadim Varganov, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects msdt.exe creating files in suspicious directories which could be a sign of exploitation of either Follina or Dogwalk vulnerabilities (source: file_event_win_msdt_susp_directories.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: File Creation In Suspicious Directory By Msdt.EXE", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Winlogon\\\\Notify\\\\logon$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:\\.dll$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may abuse features of Winlogon to execute DLLs and/or executables when a user logs in.\nWinlogon.exe is a Windows component responsible for actions at logon/logoff as well as the secure attention sequence (SAS) triggered by Ctrl-Alt-Delete.\n (source: registry_set_winlogon_notify_key.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Winlogon Notify Key Logon Persistence", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\program\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may execute their own malicious payloads by hijacking vulnerable file path references.\nAdversaries can take advantage of paths that lack surrounding quotations by placing an executable in a higher level directory within the path, so that Windows will choose the adversary's executable to ", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Creation Exe for Service with Unquoted Path", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.009"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject) and ! ($filter_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:_Classes\\\\mscfile\\\\shell\\\\open\\\\command\\\\\\(Default\\)$)'", "$filter_details: Details ~= '(?i:^%SystemRoot%\\\\system32\\\\mmc\\.exe\\ \"%1\"\\ %)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Bypasses User Account Control using Event Viewer and a relevant Windows Registry modification (source: registry_set_bypass_uac_using_eventviewer.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Bypass UAC Using Event Viewer", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.010"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\cmd\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\cscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\mshta\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\wscript\\.exe$))'", "$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Packages\\\\Microsoft\\.WindowsTerminal_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\\\LocalState\\\\settings\\.json$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the creation or modification of the Windows Terminal Profile settings file \"settings.json\" by an uncommon process. (source: file_event_win_susp_windows_terminal_profile.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Windows Terminal Profile Settings Modification By Uncommon Process", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.015"]}
