{"Condition": "(($selection_1_targetfilename) or ($selection_2_targetfilename))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\hive_sam_)|(?i:\\\\SAM\\-2021\\-)|(?i:\\\\SAM\\-2022\\-)|(?i:\\\\SAM\\-2023\\-)|(?i:\\\\SAM\\-haxx)|(?i:\\\\Sam\\.save))'", "$selection_2_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\windows\\\\temp\\\\sam$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects files written by the different tools that exploit HiveNightmare (source: file_event_win_hktl_hivenightmare_file_exports.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: HackTool - Typical HiveNightmare SAM File Export", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.001"]}
{"Condition": "($reg_image and $reg_commandline_all0 and $reg_commandline_all1 and $reg_commandline_all2 and $reg_commandline_all3) and (($hive_1_commandline_all0 and $hive_1_commandline_all1) or ($hive_2_commandline_all0 and $hive_2_commandline_all1) or ($hive_3_commandline))", "Matches": ["$reg_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\reg\\.exe$)'", "$reg_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ query\\ )'", "$reg_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/t\\ )'", "$reg_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:REG_SZ)'", "$reg_commandline_all3: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/s)'", "$hive_1_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/f\\ )'", "$hive_1_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:HKLM)'", "$hive_2_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/f\\ )'", "$hive_2_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:HKCU)'", "$hive_3_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:HKCU\\\\Software\\\\SimonTatham\\\\PuTTY\\\\Sessions)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may search the Registry on compromised systems for insecurely stored credentials.\nThe Windows Registry stores configuration information that can be used by the system or other programs.\nAdversaries may query the Registry looking for credentials and passwords that have been stored for use", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Enumeration for Credentials in Registry", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:Get\\-Process\\ lsas)|(?i:ps\\ lsas)|(?i:gps\\ lsas))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects a \"Get-Process\" cmdlet and it's aliases on lsass process, which is in almost all cases a sign of malicious activity (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_getprocess_lsass.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PowerShell Get-Process LSASS", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\\\SYSVOL\\\\)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\\\policies\\\\)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Markus Neis, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects Access to Domain Group Policies stored in SYSVOL (source: proc_creation_win_susp_sysvol_access.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious SYSVOL Domain Group Policy Access", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.006"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1 and $selection_commandline_all2 and $selection_commandline_2)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:Import\\-Certificate)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ \\-FilePath\\ )'", "$selection_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:Cert:\\\\LocalMachine\\\\Root)'", "$selection_commandline_2: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\)|(?i::\\\\Windows\\\\TEMP\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Desktop\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Downloads\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Perflogs\\\\)|(?i::\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may install a root certificate on a compromised system to avoid warnings when connecting to adversary controlled web servers. (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_import_cert_susp_locations.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Root Certificate Installed From Susp Locations", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1553.004"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_company) or ($selection_2_image) or ($selection_3_originalfilename))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_company: Company ~= '(?i:^SecurityXploded$)'", "$selection_2_image: Image ~= '(?i:PasswordDump\\.exe$)'", "$selection_3_originalfilename: OriginalFileName ~= '(?i:PasswordDump\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the execution of SecurityXploded Tools (source: proc_creation_win_hktl_secutyxploded.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 9, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: HackTool - SecurityXploded Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1555"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_description) or ($selection_2_image))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_description: Description ~= '(?i:^Web\\ Browser\\ Password\\ Viewer$)'", "$selection_2_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\WebBrowserPassView\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the execution of WebBrowserPassView.exe. A password recovery tool that reveals the passwords stored by the following Web browsers, Internet Explorer (Version 4.0 - 11.0), Mozilla Firefox (All Versions), Google Chrome, Safari, and Opera (source: proc_creation_win_pua_webbrowserpassview.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PUA - WebBrowserPassView Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1555.003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_cmdline_commandline_all0 and $selection_cmdline_commandline_all1 and $selection_cmdline_commandline_all2)", "Matches": ["$selection_cmdline_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\Lsa)'", "$selection_cmdline_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:scecli\\\\0.*)'", "$selection_cmdline_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:reg\\ add)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Sreeman", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects dropping of dll files in system32 that may be used to retrieve user credentials from LSASS (source: proc_creation_win_reg_credential_access_via_password_filter.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Dropping Of Password Filter DLL", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1556.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:UWhRCA)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:BAAAA)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the presence of \"UWhRC....AAYBAAAA\" pattern in command line.\nThe pattern \"1UWhRCAAAAA..BAAAA\" is a base64-encoded signature that corresponds to a marshaled CREDENTIAL_TARGET_INFORMATION structure.\nAttackers can use this technique to coerce authentication from victim systems to attacker-contr", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Attempts of Kerberos Coercion Via DNS SPN Spoofing", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1557.001", "T1187"]}
