{"Condition": "($selection_password_commandline) and ($selection_other_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_password_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ \\-hp)'", "$selection_other_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:\\ \\-m)|(?i:\\ a\\ ))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "@ROxPinTeddy", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the use of rar.exe, on the command line, to create an archive with password protection or with a specific compression level. This is pretty indicative of malicious actions. (source: proc_creation_win_rar_compression_with_password.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Rar Usage with Password and Compression Level", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1560.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:noconsentprompt)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:shadow:)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects RDP session hijacking by using MSTSC shadowing (source: proc_creation_win_mstsc_rdp_hijack_shadowing.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential MSTSC Shadowing Activity", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1563.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i::\\\\\\$Recycle\\.Bin\\.exe$)|(?i::\\\\Documents\\ and\\ Settings\\.exe$)|(?i::\\\\MSOCache\\.exe$)|(?i::\\\\PerfLogs\\.exe$)|(?i::\\\\Recovery\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.bat\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.sys\\.exe$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detect creation of suspicious executable file names.\nSome strings look for suspicious file extensions, others look for filenames that exploit unquoted service paths.\n (source: file_event_win_susp_executable_creation.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Executable File Creation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_targetobject_2 and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\PowerShell\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerShellCore\\\\))'", "$selection_targetobject_2: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\ModuleLogging\\\\EnableModuleLogging$)|(?i:\\\\ScriptBlockLogging\\\\EnableScriptBlockLogging$)|(?i:\\\\ScriptBlockLogging\\\\EnableScriptBlockInvocationLogging$)|(?i:\\\\Transcription\\\\EnableTranscripting$)|(?i:\\\\Transcription\\\\EnableInvocationHeader$)|(?i:\\\\EnableScripts$))'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects changes to the registry for the currently logged-in user. In order to disable PowerShell module logging, script block logging or transcription and script execution logging (source: registry_set_powershell_logging_disabled.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PowerShell Logging Disabled Via Registry Key Tampering", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.001", "T1112"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Winlogon\\\\SpecialAccounts\\\\UserList)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects modifications to the registry key \"HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\SpecialAccounts\\Userlist\" where the value is set to \"0\" in order to hide user account from being listed on the logon screen. (source: registry_set_special_accounts.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Hiding User Account Via SpecialAccounts Registry Key", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.002"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_originalfilename) or ($selection_2_commandline_all0 and $selection_2_commandline_all1) or ($selection_3_commandline_all0 and $selection_3_commandline_all1 and $selection_3_commandline_all2))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_originalfilename: OriginalFileName ~= '(?i:^AdvancedRun\\.exe$)'", "$selection_2_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /EXEFilename\\ )'", "$selection_2_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /Run)'", "$selection_3_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /WindowState\\ 0)'", "$selection_3_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /RunAs\\ )'", "$selection_3_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /CommandLine\\ )'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the execution of AdvancedRun utility (source: proc_creation_win_pua_advancedrun.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PUA - AdvancedRun Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.003", "T1134.002", "T1059.003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_parentimage and $selection_image and $selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_parentimage: ParentImage ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$))'", "$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$))'", "$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:Get\\-Content)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\-Stream)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Sergey Soldatov, Kaspersky Lab, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects PowerShell script execution from Alternate Data Stream (ADS) (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_run_script_from_ads.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Run PowerShell Script from ADS", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_parentimage and $selection_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_parentimage: ParentImage ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Winrar\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\7zFM\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\peazip\\.exe$))'", "$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\isoburn\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\PowerISO\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\ImgBurn\\.exe$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects cases in which an ISO files is opend within an archiver like 7Zip or Winrar, which is a sign of phishing as threat actors put small ISO files in archives as email attachments to bypass certain filters and protective measures (mark of web) (source: proc_creation_win_susp_archiver_iso_phishing", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Phishing Pattern ISO in Archive", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1566"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\.exe$)|(?i:______\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.doc\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.doc\\.js$)|(?i:\\.docx\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.docx\\.js$)|(?i:\\.gif\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.jpeg\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.jpg\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.mkv\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.mov\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.mp3\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.mp4\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.pdf\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.pdf\\.js$)|(?i:\\.png\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.ppt\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.ppt\\.js$)|(?i:\\.pptx\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.pptx\\.js$)|(?i:\\.rtf\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.rtf\\.js$)|(?i:\\.svg\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.txt\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.txt\\.js$)|(?i:\\.xls\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.xls\\.js$)|(?i:\\.xlsx\\.exe$)|(?i:\\.xlsx\\.js$)|(?i:\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\\.exe$))'", "$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\.exe)|(?i:______\\.exe)|(?i:\\.doc\\.exe)|(?i:\\.doc\\.js)|(?i:\\.docx\\.exe)|(?i:\\.docx\\.js)|(?i:\\.gif\\.exe)|(?i:\\.jpeg\\.exe)|(?i:\\.jpg\\.exe)|(?i:\\.mkv\\.exe)|(?i:\\.mov\\.exe)|(?i:\\.mp3\\.exe)|(?i:\\.mp4\\.exe)|(?i:\\.pdf\\.exe)|(?i:\\.pdf\\.js)|(?i:\\.png\\.exe)|(?i:\\.ppt\\.exe)|(?i:\\.ppt\\.js)|(?i:\\.pptx\\.exe)|(?i:\\.pptx\\.js)|(?i:\\.rtf\\.exe)|(?i:\\.rtf\\.js)|(?i:\\.svg\\.exe)|(?i:\\.txt\\.exe)|(?i:\\.txt\\.js)|(?i:\\.xls\\.exe)|(?i:\\.xls\\.js)|(?i:\\.xlsx\\.exe)|(?i:\\.xlsx\\.js)|(?i:\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\u2800\\.exe))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), @blu3_team (idea), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects suspicious use of an .exe extension after a non-executable file extension like .pdf.exe, a set of spaces or underlines to cloak the executable file in spear phishing campaigns (source: proc_creation_win_susp_double_extension.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Double Extension File Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1566.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_destinationhostname)", "Matches": ["$selection_destinationhostname: DestinationHostname ~= '(?:(?i:tunnel\\.us\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.eu\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.ap\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.au\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.sa\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.jp\\.ngrok\\.com)|(?i:tunnel\\.in\\.ngrok\\.com))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects an executable initiating a network connection to \"ngrok\" tunneling domains.\nAttackers were seen using this \"ngrok\" in order to store their second stage payloads and malware.\nWhile communication with such domains can be legitimate, often times is a sign of either data exfiltration by maliciou", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [3], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Communication To Ngrok Tunneling Service Initiated", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1567", "T1568.002", "T1572", "T1090", "T1102"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_initiated and $selection_destinationhostname)", "Matches": ["$selection_initiated: Initiated ~= '(?i:^true$)'", "$selection_destinationhostname: DestinationHostname ~= '(?i:\\.devtunnels\\.ms$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Kamran Saifullah", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects network connections to Devtunnels domains initiated by a process on a system. Attackers can abuse that feature to establish a reverse shell or persistence on a machine.\n (source: net_connection_win_domain_devtunnels.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [3], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Network Connection Initiated To DevTunnels Domain", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1567.001", "T1572"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename_all0 and $selection_targetfilename_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename_all0: TargetFilename ~= '(?i::\\\\Users\\\\)'", "$selection_targetfilename_all1: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\\\.config\\\\rclone\\\\)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Aaron Greetham (@beardofbinary) - NCC Group", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects Rclone config files being created (source: file_event_win_rclone_config_files.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Rclone Config File Creation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1567.002"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_image) or ($selection_2_originalfilename))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\psexec\\.exe$)'", "$selection_2_originalfilename: OriginalFileName ~= '(?i:^psexec\\.c$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "omkar72", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects user accept agreement execution in psexec commandline (source: proc_creation_win_sysinternals_psexec_execution.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Psexec Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1569", "T1021"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ runassystem\\ )'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the use of NirCmd tool for command execution as SYSTEM user (source: proc_creation_win_pua_nircmd_as_system.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PUA - NirCmd Execution As LOCAL SYSTEM", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1569.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_destinationhostname and $selection_initiated)", "Matches": ["$selection_destinationhostname: DestinationHostname ~= '(?:(?i:\\.localto\\.net$)|(?i:\\.localtonet\\.com$))'", "$selection_initiated: Initiated ~= '(?i:^true$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Andreas Braathen (mnemonic.io)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects an executable initiating a network connection to \"LocaltoNet\" tunneling sub-domains.\nLocaltoNet is a reverse proxy that enables localhost services to be exposed to the Internet.\nAttackers have been seen to use this service for command-and-control activities to bypass MFA and perimeter contro", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [3], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Communication To LocaltoNet Tunneling Service Initiated", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1572", "T1090", "T1102"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\register\\-cimprovider\\.exe$)'", "$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\-path)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:dll)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Ivan Dyachkov, Yulia Fomina, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects using register-cimprovider.exe to execute arbitrary dll file. (source: proc_creation_win_registry_cimprovider_dll_load.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: DLL Execution Via Register-cimprovider.exe", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_imageloaded) and ! ($filter_imageloaded)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\arubanetsvc\\.exe$)'", "$selection_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\wtsapi32\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\msvcr100\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\msvcp100\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\dbghelp\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\dbgcore\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\wininet\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\iphlpapi\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\version\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\cryptsp\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\cryptbase\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\wldp\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\profapi\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\sspicli\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\winsta\\.dll$)|(?i:\\\\dpapi\\.dll$))'", "$filter_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?:(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\)|(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\SysWOW64\\\\)|(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\WinSxS\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects potential DLL sideloading activity via the Aruba Networks Virtual Intranet Access \"arubanetsvc.exe\" process using DLL Search Order Hijacking (source: image_load_side_load_aruba_networks_virtual_intranet_access.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [7], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Aruba Network Service Potential DLL Sideloading", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_imageloaded)", "Matches": ["$selection_imageloaded: ImageLoaded ~= '(?:(?i::\\\\Windows\\ \\\\System32\\\\)|(?i::\\\\Windows\\ \\\\SysWOW64\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects DLLs loading from a spoofed Windows directory path with an extra space (e.g \"C:\\Windows \\System32\") which can bypass Windows trusted path verification.\nThis technique tricks Windows into treating the path as trusted, allowing malicious DLLs to load with high integrity privileges bypassing UA", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [7], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Trusted Path Bypass via Windows Directory Spoofing", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574.007", "T1548.002"]}
{"Condition": "! ($system_utility_image) and ($parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all0 and $parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all1 and $parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all2)", "Matches": ["$system_utility_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\)|(?i:^C:\\\\Windows\\\\SysWOW64\\\\))'", "$parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all0: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:cmd\\.exe\\ /c)'", "$parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all1: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:RoamDiag\\.cmd)'", "$parent_is_settingsynchost_parentcommandline_all2: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:\\-outputpath)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Anton Kutepov, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects using SettingSyncHost.exe to run hijacked binary (source: proc_creation_win_lolbin_settingsynchost.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Using SettingSyncHost.exe as LOLBin", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574.008"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_integritylevel and $selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1 and $selection_commandline_2)", "Matches": ["$selection_integritylevel: IntegrityLevel ~= '(?:(?i:^Medium$)|(?i:^S\\-1\\-16\\-8192$))'", "$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:ControlSet)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:services)'", "$selection_commandline_2: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\ImagePath)|(?i:\\\\FailureCommand)|(?i:\\\\ServiceDll))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Teymur Kheirkhabarov", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detect modification of services configuration (ImagePath, FailureCommand and ServiceDLL) in registry by processes with Medium integrity level (source: proc_creation_win_registry_privilege_escalation_via_service_key.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Privilege Escalation via Service Permissions Weakness", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574.011"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\brave\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\chrome\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\firefox\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\iexplore\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\maxthon\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\MicrosoftEdge\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\msedge\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\msedgewebview2\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\opera\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\safari\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\seamonkey\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\vivaldi\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\whale\\.exe$))'", "$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\.vhd)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113, Christopher Peacock '@securepeacock', SCYTHE '@scythe_io'", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects creation of \".vhd\"/\".vhdx\" files by browser processes.\nMalware can use mountable Virtual Hard Disk \".vhd\" files to encapsulate payloads and evade security controls.\n (source: file_event_win_vhd_download_via_browsers.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: VHD Image Download Via Browser", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1587.001"]}
