{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Software\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ Script\\\\Settings\\\\AmsiEnable$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects attempts to disable AMSI (Anti-Malware Scan Interface) by modifying the AmsiEnable registry value.\nAnti-Malware Scan Interface (AMSI) is a security feature in Windows that allows applications and services to integrate with anti-malware products for enhanced protection against malicious conte", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: AMSI Disabled via Registry Modification", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1685"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:/logon:none)|(?i:/system:none)|(?i:/sam:none)|(?i:/privilege:none)|(?i:/object:none)|(?i:/process:none)|(?i:/policy:none))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Threat actors can use an older version of the auditpol binary available inside the NT resource kit to change audit policy configuration to impair detection capability.\nThis can be carried out by selectively disabling/removing certain audit policies as well as restoring a custom policy owned by the t", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Audit Policy Tampering Via NT Resource Kit Auditpol", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1685.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject_all0 and $selection_targetobject_all1 and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject_all0: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Services\\\\SharedAccess\\\\Parameters\\\\FirewallPolicy\\\\)'", "$selection_targetobject_all1: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\AuthorizedApplications\\\\List)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i::Enabled:)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the degradation of the system firewall security by the creation or re-enabling of per-application\nexceptions via registry writes to the AuthorizedApplications\\List keys under FirewallPolicy, which grants\nthe targeted executable network access and can be abused by malware to bypass network re", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Add Authorized Applications to Microsoft Defender Firewall via Registry", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1686.003"]}
