{"Condition": "($selection_parentimage and $selection_parentcommandline_all0 and $selection_parentcommandline_all1 and $selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_parentimage: ParentImage ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\svchost\\.exe$)'", "$selection_parentcommandline_all0: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:\\-k\\ netsvcs)'", "$selection_parentcommandline_all1: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:\\-s\\ Schedule)'", "$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:\\ \\-windowstyle\\ hidden$)|(?i:\\ \\-w\\ hidden$)|(?i:\\ \\-ep\\ bypass$)|(?i:\\ \\-noni$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "pH-T (Nextron Systems), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects suspicious powershell execution via a schedule task where the command ends with an suspicious flags to hide the powershell instance instead of executeing scripts or commands. This could be a sign of persistence via PowerShell \"Get-Variable\" technique as seen being used in Colibri Loader (sou", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Persistence Via Powershell Search Order Hijacking - Task", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1053.005", "T1059.001"]}
