81dbdb4e8e95e2ad2c127)|(?i:IMPHASH=4c7cc13a110ccdbb932bb9d7d42efdf4)|(?i:IMPHASH=45bfe170e0cd654bc1e2ae3fca3ac3f4)|(?i:IMPHASH=3db9de43d5d530c10d0cd2d43c7a0771))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects loading of known malicious drivers via their hash. (source: driver_load_win_mal_drivers.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [6], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Malicious Driver Load", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1543.003", "T1068"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\Get\\-Variable\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Get-Variable is a valid PowerShell cmdlet\nWindowsApps is by default in the path where PowerShell is executed.\nSo when the Get-Variable command is issued on PowerShell execution, the system first looks for the Get-Variable executable in the path and executes the malicious binary instead of looking fo", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Get-Variable.exe Creation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546", "T1027"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename_all0 and $selection_targetfilename_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename_all0: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\\\\\127\\.0\\.0)'", "$selection_targetfilename_all1: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\ADMIN\\$\\\\)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Aversaries may use to interact with a remote network share using Server Message Block (SMB).\nThis technique is used by post-exploitation frameworks.\n (source: file_event_win_writing_local_admin_share.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Writing Local Admin Share", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:^C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\system32\\\\wbem\\\\scrcons\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Thomas Patzke", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects file writes of WMI script event consumer (source: file_event_win_wmi_persistence_script_event_consumer_write.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: WMI Persistence - Script Event Consumer File Write", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_parentimage and $selection_image and $selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_parentimage: ParentImage ~= '(?i:\\\\winlogon\\.exe$)'", "$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\cmd\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\cscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\mshta\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\regsvr32\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\rundll32\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\wscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\wt\\.exe$))'", "$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:sethc\\.exe)|(?i:utilman\\.exe)|(?i:osk\\.exe)|(?i:Magnify\\.exe)|(?i:Narrator\\.exe)|(?i:DisplaySwitch\\.exe))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), @twjackomo, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the usage and installation of a backdoor that uses an option to register a malicious debugger for built-in tools that are accessible in the login screen (source: proc_creation_win_cmd_sticky_key_like_backdoor_execution.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 9, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Sticky Key Like Backdoor Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.008"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\AppCompatFlags\\\\Layers\\\\)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:REGISTERAPPRESTART)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the setting of the REGISTERAPPRESTART compatibility layer on an application.\nThis compatibility layer allows an application to register for restart using the \"RegisterApplicationRestart\" API.\nThis can be potentially abused as a persistence mechanism.\n (source: registry_set_persistence_app_cp", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Persistence Via AppCompat RegisterAppRestart Layer", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.011"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\.VSCode_profile\\.ps1$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the creation or modification of a vscode related powershell profile which could indicate suspicious activity as the profile can be used as a mean of persistence (source: file_event_win_susp_vscode_powershell_profile.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: VsCode Powershell Profile Modification", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1546.013"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:grpconv\\.exe\\ \\-o)|(?i:grpconv\\ \\-o))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the suspicious execution of a utility to convert Windows 3.x .grp files or for persistence purposes by malicious software or actors (source: proc_creation_win_lolbin_susp_grpconv.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious GrpConv Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_targetfilename and $selection_targetfilename_2)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$))'", "$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\start\\ menu\\\\programs\\\\startup\\\\)'", "$selection_targetfilename_2: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\.lnk$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Christopher Peacock '@securepeacock', SCYTHE", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects PowerShell writing startup shortcuts.\nThis procedure was highlighted in Red Canary Intel Insights Oct. 2021, \"We frequently observe adversaries using PowerShell to write malicious .lnk files into the startup directory to establish persistence.\nAccordingly, this detection opportunity is likel", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Startup Shortcut Persistence Via PowerShell.EXE", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i::\\\\Windows\\\\apppatch\\\\Custom\\\\)|(?i::\\\\Windows\\\\apppatch\\\\CustomSDB\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may establish persistence and/or elevate privileges by executing malicious content triggered by application shims.\nThe Microsoft Windows Application Compatibility Infrastructure/Framework (Application Shim) was created to allow for backward compatibility of software as the operating syst", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: New Custom Shim Database Created", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1547.009"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_parentimage and $selection_parentcommandline) and ! ($filter_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_parentimage: ParentImage ~= '(?i:\\\\mmc\\.exe$)'", "$selection_parentcommandline: ParentCommandLine ~= '(?i:WF\\.msc)'", "$filter_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\WerFault\\.exe$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects attempts to bypass User Account Control (UAC) by hijacking the Microsoft Management Console (MMC) Windows Firewall snap-in (source: proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_hijacking_firwall_snap_in.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: UAC Bypass via Windows Firewall Snap-In Hijack", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1548"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:C:\\\\Windows\\ \\\\System32\\\\)|(?i:C:\\\\Windows\\ \\\\SysWOW64\\\\))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects indicators of a UAC bypass method by mocking directories (source: proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_trustedpath.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 9, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: TrustedPath UAC Bypass Pattern", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1548.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:ConsoleHost_history\\.txt)|(?i:\\(Get\\-PSReadLineOption\\)\\.HistorySavePath))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Luc G\u00e9naux", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects potential access attempts to the PowerShell console history directly via history file (ConsoleHost_history.txt).\nThis can give access to plaintext passwords used in PowerShell commands or used for general reconnaissance.\n (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_console_history_file_access.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential PowerShell Console History Access Attempt via History File", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:Export\\-PfxCertificate\\ )|(?i:Export\\-Certificate\\ ))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects calls to cmdlets that are used to export certificates from the local certificate store. Threat actors were seen abusing this to steal private keys from compromised machines. (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_export_certificate.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Certificate Exported Via PowerShell", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1552.004", "T1059.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?:(?i:X509Enrollment\\.CBinaryConverter)|(?i:884e2002\\-217d\\-11da\\-b2a4\\-000e7bbb2b09))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detect use of X509Enrollment (source: proc_creation_win_powershell_x509enrollment.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious X509Enrollment - Process Creation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1553.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename and $selection_targetfilename_2)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:ntds_capi_)|(?i:ntds_legacy_)|(?i:ntds_unknown_))'", "$selection_targetfilename_2: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:\\.cer$)|(?i:\\.key$)|(?i:\\.pfx$)|(?i:\\.pvk$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nounou Mbeiri, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects file names with specific patterns seen generated and used by tools such as Mimikatz and DSInternals related to exported or stolen DPAPI backup keys and certificates.\n (source: file_event_win_susp_dpapi_backup_and_cert_export_ioc.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: DPAPI Backup Keys And Certificate Export Activity IOC", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1555", "T1552.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ \\-\\-adcs\\ )'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ \\-\\-port\\ )'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects command line parameters used by ADCSPwn, a tool to escalate privileges in an active directory network by coercing authenticate from machine accounts and relaying to the certificate service (source: proc_creation_win_hktl_adcspwn.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: HackTool - ADCSPwn Execution", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1557.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\ /dest:rdp\\-tcp\\#)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects a suspicious RDP session redirect using tscon.exe (source: proc_creation_win_tscon_rdp_redirect.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious RDP Redirect Using TSCON", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1563.002", "T1021.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\CrashControl)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Tobias Michalski (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects disabling the CrashDump per registry (as used by HermeticWiper) (source: registry_set_crashdump_disabled.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: CrashControl CrashDump Disabled", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564", "T1112"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Explorer\\\\Advanced\\\\ShowSuperHidden$)|(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Explorer\\\\Advanced\\\\Hidden$))'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects modifications to the \"Hidden\" and \"ShowSuperHidden\" explorer registry values in order to disable showing of hidden files and system files.\nThis technique is abused by several malware families to hide their files from normal users.\n (source: registry_set_hide_file.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Displaying Hidden Files Feature Disabled", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline_all0 and $selection_commandline_all1 and $selection_commandline_all2 and $selection_commandline_all3)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\reg\\.exe$)'", "$selection_commandline_all0: CommandLine ~= '(?i:\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\ NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Winlogon\\\\SpecialAccounts\\\\UserList)'", "$selection_commandline_all1: CommandLine ~= '(?i:add)'", "$selection_commandline_all2: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/v)'", "$selection_commandline_all3: CommandLine ~= '(?i:/d\\ 0)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "@Kostastsale, TheDFIRReport", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects changes to the registry key \"HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\SpecialAccounts\\Userlist\" where the value is set to \"0\" in order to hide user account from being listed on the logon screen.\n (source: proc_creation_win_registry_special_accounts_hide_user.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Hiding User Account Via SpecialAccounts Registry Key - CommandLine", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetfilename)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:::\\$index_allocation)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Scoubi (@ScoubiMtl)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the creation of hidden file/folder with the \"::$index_allocation\" stream. Which can be used as a technique to prevent access to folder and files from tooling such as \"explorer.exe\" and \"powershell.exe\"\n (source: file_event_win_susp_hidden_dir_index_allocation.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Hidden Directory Creation Via NTFS INDEX_ALLOCATION Stream", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1564.004"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_targetfilename and $selection_targetfilename_2_all0 and $selection_targetfilename_2_all1 and $selection_targetfilename_3) and ! ($filter_image and $filter_targetfilename_all0 and $filter_targetfilename_all1 and $filter_targetfilename_all2 and $filter_targetfilename_all3)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\winword\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\excel\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\powerpnt\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\MSACCESS\\.EXE$)|(?i:\\\\MSPUB\\.EXE$)|(?i:\\\\fltldr\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\cmd\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\certutil\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\mshta\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\cscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\wscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\curl\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\powershell\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\pwsh\\.exe$))'", "$selection_targetfilename: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\.dll$)'", "$selection_targetfilename_2_all0: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\Users\\\\)'", "$selection_targetfilename_2_all1: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\AppData\\\\)'", "$selection_targetfilename_3: TargetFilename ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\OneDrive\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\ OneDrive\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\Teams\\\\)|(?i:\\\\Local\\\\slack\\\\app\\-)|(?i:\\\\Local\\\\Programs\\\\Microsoft\\ VS\\ Code\\\\))'", "$filter_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\cmd\\.exe$)'", "$filter_targetfilename_all0: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\Users\\\\)'", "$filter_targetfilename_all1: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\AppData\\\\)'", "$filter_targetfilename_all2: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\OneDrive\\\\)'", "$filter_targetfilename_all3: TargetFilename ~= '(?i:\\\\api\\-ms\\-win\\-core\\-)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Tim Rauch (rule), Elastic (idea)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects attempts to create a DLL file to a known desktop application dependencies folder such as Slack, Teams or OneDrive and by an unusual process. This may indicate an attempt to load a malicious module via DLL search order hijacking. (source: file_event_win_initial_access_dll_search_order_hijacki", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [11], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Initial Access via DLL Search Order Hijacking", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1566", "T1566.001", "T1574", "T1574.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\Temporary\\ Internet\\ Files\\\\Content\\.Outlook\\\\)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects a suspicious program execution in Outlook temp folder (source: proc_creation_win_office_outlook_execution_from_temp.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Execution From Outlook Temporary Folder", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1566.001"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_initiated and $selection_destinationhostname)", "Matches": ["$selection_initiated: Initiated ~= '(?i:^true$)'", "$selection_destinationhostname: DestinationHostname ~= '(?:(?i:\\.ngrok\\-free\\.app$)|(?i:\\.ngrok\\-free\\.dev$)|(?i:\\.ngrok\\.app$)|(?i:\\.ngrok\\.dev$)|(?i:\\.ngrok\\.io$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects an executable initiating a network connection to \"ngrok\" domains.\nAttackers were seen using this \"ngrok\" in order to store their second stage payloads and malware.\nWhile communication with such domains can be legitimate, often times is a sign of either data exfiltration by malicious actors o", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [3], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Process Initiated Network Connection To Ngrok Domain", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1567", "T1572", "T1102"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_targetobject_2 and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Services\\\\)'", "$selection_targetobject_2: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\ImagePath$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?:(?i:powershell)|(?i:pwsh))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "oscd.community, Natalia Shornikova", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects that a powershell code is written to the registry as a service. (source: registry_set_powershell_as_service.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: PowerShell as a Service in Registry", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1569.002"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_image and $selection_commandline)", "Matches": ["$selection_image: Image ~= '(?i:\\\\ssh\\.exe$)'", "$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i::3389)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Execution of ssh.exe to perform data exfiltration and tunneling through RDP (source: proc_creation_win_ssh_rdp_tunneling.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential RDP Tunneling Via SSH", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1572"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject) and ! ($filter_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Microsoft\\\\\\.NETFramework\\\\DbgManagedDebugger$)'", "$filter_details: Details ~= '(?i:^\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\system32\\\\vsjitdebugger\\.exe\"\\ PID\\ %d\\ APPDOM\\ %d\\ EXTEXT\\ \"%s\"\\ EVTHDL\\ %d$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the addition of the \"Debugger\" value to the \"DbgManagedDebugger\" key in order to achieve persistence. Which will get invoked when an application crashes (source: registry_set_dbgmanageddebugger_persistence.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Potential Registry Persistence Attempt Via DbgManagedDebugger", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\Services\\\\DHCPServer\\\\Parameters\\\\CalloutDlls$)|(?i:\\\\Services\\\\DHCPServer\\\\Parameters\\\\CalloutEnabled$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Dimitrios Slamaris", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the installation of a Callout DLL via CalloutDlls and CalloutEnabled parameter in Registry, which can be used to execute code in context of the DHCP server (restart required) (source: registry_set_dhcp_calloutdll.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: DHCP Callout DLL Installation", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1574.001", "T1112"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_company)", "Matches": ["$selection_company: Company ~= '(?i:^Cube0x0$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the execution of different Windows based hacktools via PE metadata (company, product, etc.) even if the files have been renamed (source: proc_creation_win_hktl_execution_via_pe_metadata.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Hacktool Execution - PE Metadata", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1588.002", "T1003"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_commandline) and ! ($filter_image)", "Matches": ["$selection_commandline: CommandLine ~= '(?i:gatherNetworkInfo\\.vbs)'", "$filter_image: Image ~= '(?:(?i:\\\\cscript\\.exe$)|(?i:\\\\wscript\\.exe$))'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects execution of the built-in script located in \"C:\\Windows\\System32\\gatherNetworkInfo.vbs\". Which can be used to gather information about the target machine (source: proc_creation_win_susp_gather_network_info_execution.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [1], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Suspicious Reconnaissance Activity Via GatherNetworkInfo.VBS", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1615", "T1059.005"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\FilterManager\\\\FltmgrDevDriveAllowAntivirusFilter$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "@kostastsale, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects activity that indicates a user disabling the ability for Antivirus mini filter to inspect a \"Dev Drive\".\n (source: registry_set_devdrv_disallow_antivirus_filter.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Antivirus Filter Driver Disallowed On Dev Drive - Registry", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1685"]}
{"Condition": "(($selection_1_targetobject and $selection_1_eventtype) or ($selection_2_newname))", "Matches": ["$selection_1_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:^HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\MiniNt$)'", "$selection_1_eventtype: EventType ~= '(?i:^CreateKey$)'", "$selection_2_newname: NewName ~= '(?i:^HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\MiniNt$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "Ilyas Ochkov, oscd.community", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Detects the addition of a key 'MiniNt' to the registry. Upon a reboot, Windows Event Log service will stop writing events. (source: registry_event_disable_security_events_logging_adding_reg_key_minint.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 8, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Disable Security Events Logging Adding Reg Key MiniNt", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1685.001", "T1112"]}
{"Condition": "($selection_targetobject and $selection_targetobject_2 and $selection_details)", "Matches": ["$selection_targetobject: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\Services\\\\SharedAccess\\\\Parameters\\\\FirewallPolicy\\\\)'", "$selection_targetobject_2: TargetObject ~= '(?i:\\\\EnableFirewall$)'", "$selection_details: Details ~= '(?i:^DWORD\\ \\(0x00000000\\)$)'"], "Meta": {"Author": "frack113", "Channels": ["Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"], "Comment": "Adversaries may disable or modify system firewalls in order to bypass controls limiting network usage (source: registry_set_disable_defender_firewall.yml)", "Computers": [], "Criticality": 6, "EventIDs": [12, 13, 14], "Schema": "1.0.0"}, "Name": "Sigma: Disable Microsoft Defender Firewall via Registry", "Tags": ["Sigma", "SigmaHQ", "T1686.003"]}
